error-nm-unavailable = NetworkManager could not be reached or access was denied.
error-nm-rejected = NetworkManager rejected the profile change. Check authorization and saved settings.
error-nm-timeout = NetworkManager did not confirm the write. Check its saved profiles before retrying; the change may have completed.
error-nm-stale = NetworkManager state changed. Refresh the connection list before trying again.
error-nm-control = NetworkManager refused the connection request. Check authorization and VPN service settings.
error-nm-control-timeout = NetworkManager did not confirm the connection request. Refresh its state; do not retry automatically.
error-nm-update-unsupported = Profile changes require a fresh versioned NetworkManager observation (NM 1.44 or newer). Refresh before changing profiles; no unconditional fallback is allowed.
error-url = Enter an HTTPS subscription URL without a username, password or fragment.
error-download = Could not load the subscription. Check the URL, TLS certificate and server response. Redirects are not followed.
error-download-timeout = Subscription download timed out. The previous profile list is unchanged.
error-source-too-large = The subscription exceeds the 2 MiB size limit.
error-source-too-many = The subscription contains more than 512 records.
error-source-format = The subscription does not match the selected format. Expected a complete JSON configuration or, in explicit node-only mode, a URI list. No profiles were imported.
error-complete-required = The server did not return a complete configuration. Node-only import must be selected explicitly; no fallback was attempted.
error-policy-fakeip = The complete configuration requires FakeIP DNS semantics this importer cannot yet preserve. No profiles were extracted.
error-policy-dns = The complete configuration has DNS settings this version cannot preserve. No profiles were extracted.
error-policy-routing = The complete configuration has routing settings this version cannot preserve. No profiles were extracted.
error-policy-client = The complete configuration requires unsupported client integration settings. No profiles were extracted.
error-policy-configuration = The complete configuration is outside the supported native IPv4 policy contract. No profiles were extracted or policies discarded.
error-resolver = Choose the current network DNS or a public IPv4 DNS server through the VPN.
error-dns-policy = This DNS override is incompatible with the routing policy. Direct hostname rules cannot yet use a manual through-VPN resolver; choose current network DNS instead.
